WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.030 --> 00:00:03.419
One of the crucial skills that you can
acquire nowadays is learning how to

00:00:03.419 --> 00:00:07.350
learn and this concerns language
learning and anything else. But there is

00:00:07.350 --> 00:00:11.610
one aspect that is often neglected
within the language learning world and

00:00:11.610 --> 00:00:17.400
it is getting ready to learn, how to get
the setup correct before you start

00:00:17.400 --> 00:00:21.660
learning anything. Hi my name is Luca
from LucaLampariello.com and today I'm

00:00:21.660 --> 00:00:30.720
going to show you how I get ready to
learn any language. We know that building

00:00:30.720 --> 00:00:33.750
habits is crucial when you want to learn
anything and you want to do it for a

00:00:33.750 --> 00:00:38.010
long time but the problem is it's
difficult to stick to your habits so one

00:00:38.010 --> 00:00:41.730
thing that you want to keep in mind is
that when you start learning languages

00:00:41.730 --> 00:00:45.930
and you have and you want to learn
languages every day, make sure that

00:00:45.930 --> 00:00:50.399
you see the object that you're going to
use the language material, the book

00:00:50.399 --> 00:00:54.570
photocopies - you name it - just visible
when you wake up in the morning or when

00:00:54.570 --> 00:00:59.879
the moment comes to learn, because that
will remind you "okay that's the time to

00:00:59.879 --> 00:01:04.559
learn". So, one thing that is very easy to
do and it's a huge reminder of learning

00:01:04.559 --> 00:01:08.880
is that I keep all my language learning
material on my desktop, because that's

00:01:08.880 --> 00:01:12.450
where I sit down and that's where I
start learning every single day when I

00:01:12.450 --> 00:01:14.780
wake up.

00:01:16.650 --> 00:01:21.939
Okay so, I'm sitting down and I'm ready
to learn. What is it that I do? First, I

00:01:21.939 --> 00:01:26.890
have my computer on the left, second I
have my language material on the right, I

00:01:26.890 --> 00:01:30.670
always make sure that I have some paper
based material, because I really like

00:01:30.670 --> 00:01:33.640
paper based and he keeps me focused
- we're going to talk about this in a

00:01:33.640 --> 00:01:37.240
second - so what I do is that I use my computer

00:01:37.240 --> 00:01:43.930
to listen to some audio files, and in the
meanwhile, I just mark words or mark the

00:01:43.930 --> 00:01:48.700
the intonation of the language on the right
so in this position it's really easy to

00:01:48.700 --> 00:01:53.140
do two things at the same time: on the
one hand literally - better - with my left

00:01:53.140 --> 00:01:56.979
hand I'm just stopping the audio on and
off when they need to, and with my right

00:01:56.979 --> 00:02:01.149
hand, I'm just looking at a piece of
paper marking the intonation potentially

00:02:01.149 --> 00:02:05.080
of the text and also marking words for
vocabulary. So I can do two things at the

00:02:05.080 --> 00:02:08.610
same time with both hands

00:02:10.790 --> 00:02:16.260
But there's one last thing there really
makes a difference and without this

00:02:16.260 --> 00:02:21.570
nothing is useful in a way. You want to
stay focused. When we talk about having

00:02:21.570 --> 00:02:26.160
or finding time, that's just one piece of
the framework, of the entire picture. The

00:02:26.160 --> 00:02:29.850
reality is that there are two other
important factors and they're energy and

00:02:29.850 --> 00:02:34.290
concentration. In particular,
concentration is so important nowadays

00:02:34.290 --> 00:02:38.700
because we live in a world full of
distractions. So the very first thing

00:02:38.700 --> 00:02:42.900
that I do is I turn off my phone or I
put it in flying mode because your phone is

00:02:42.900 --> 00:02:47.190
a main source of distraction, and oh - one
other thing - don't look at your phone as

00:02:47.190 --> 00:02:50.430
soon as you wake up - it really distracts
you - you want to stay focused on tasks

00:02:50.430 --> 00:02:54.360
and just hit languages if you are an
early morning person and you learn

00:02:54.360 --> 00:03:02.550
languages first thing in the morning. So
the first point is if you want to get

00:03:02.550 --> 00:03:07.050
into the habit of learning, you better
have some visual cues just in front of

00:03:07.050 --> 00:03:10.020
you when you wake up, when you when you start learning, because that's very

00:03:10.020 --> 00:03:14.880
important and it's an easy reminder of
oh that's the moment to learn. The second

00:03:14.880 --> 00:03:18.420
point is getting to the right position
and get the right tools for learning.

00:03:18.420 --> 00:03:23.400
Remember: technology can be your master
or can be your slave and if you want to

00:03:23.400 --> 00:03:27.330
technology to be at your service,
you better use technology the right way.

00:03:27.330 --> 00:03:31.590
And the third point is make sure that
you eliminate all the possible

00:03:31.590 --> 00:03:36.000
distractions, all the possible obstacles
that keep you from being focused from

00:03:36.000 --> 00:03:39.930
stay focused for at least 30 minutes
because you have to remember that it's

00:03:39.930 --> 00:03:45.420
not just about time it's also about your
energy and about your concentration. So

00:03:45.420 --> 00:03:48.390
there you have it. If you want to know
more just click in the description box

